{"id": "idaho-2", "headline": "Dean Cameron to lead Idaho Health and Welfare for now", "source": "Idaho Capital Sun", "url": "https://idahocapitalsun.com/2026/11/25/former-idaho-senator-and-insurance-director-to-lead-state-health-and-welfare-agency-for-now/", "published": "2026-11-25", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Gov. Brad Little announced Wednesday that Idaho Department of Insurance Director Dean Cameron will serve as interim director of the Idaho Department of Health and Welfare starting Nov. 30. Cameron held the same interim role in 2024. Weston Trexler will be interim insurance director. Little expects to choose a permanent Health and Welfare director after the 2027 legislative session, which begins Jan. 11. Former director Juliet Charron stepped down after just over a year. During the session, Cameron will work with lawmakers on a proposal to restore budget cuts for disability caregivers. The agency has more than 3,000 employees and a budget above 5 billion dollars, mostly federal.", "It runs Medicaid, SNAP and WIC. Cameron was a state senator for 25 years before leading the insurance department. Source: Idaho Capital Sun."], "qr": {"n": 41, "rows": ["11111110011010101111100110100111101111111", "10000010101001011000001000111000001000001", "10111010001110001000110000101000101011101", "10111010110101001100001011000100001011101", "10111010011110001011000100001011001011101", "10000010110111011010101001010010101000001", "11111110101010101010101010101010101111111", "00000000001110001000111010011001100000000", "11111011110001000100001001010101110101010", "01101100110011001011110111100111111111011", "11100011110110110010111010111000100010000", "01010000011010111000010110111010000111000", "10000110011101110101000011101101000001110", "00101100111011001111110100001111111111101", "01011111100000110010001000011000010000100", "10100101001010101011010000010010100011010", "01010111010001111100001101010100000000100", "11010100001101001011100111101001111110011", "1110111000